# On Mars now
do ScoreManager.set_demo_music("res://music/mars.ogg")
[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/mars_landscape.png" fade="0.0"]
[style name="Dialogue"]
Narrator: The makeshift escape pod heats up as it plummets to the ground faster and faster. Sweat drips from the outside of MC’s helmet, their grip tightening with the speed increasing.
Narrator: Looking outside the window in pursuit of some grandiose, life-ending comforting sight, you see the beautiful Martian landscape, as well as the remnants of the station coming apart.
mainChar: {Blue} At least the view is nice, however short the time I get to enjoy it is.
# (Art shows objects floating, then transition to flying around randomly)
Narrator: Suddenly, the pod starts spinning, throwing everything inside around at random. Tools, freeze dried food, and various other items fly around as MC holds on. Lasting only for a few moments, the pod stabilizes upon entering orbit.
mainChar: {Blue} I feel, SO nauseous right now.\
\
*gurgle/retch*\
\
Oh god hold it in hold it in hold it in
Narrator: Managing to keep that bit of space sick out of your helmet, a little breath of relief comes out of your pursed lips.\
The relief is short lived.\
As the pod plummets through the Martian sky, MC can’t help but wonder…
mainChar: How miserable has this trip been?
